From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: make GLINK and SMD edge stop retryable

The core stops subdevices before the PAS stop callback. If PAS reports an
error, a later stop request visits those subdevices again. Both native
transport unregister functions dereference their argument, but the first
successful stop clears the stored edge. Do not unregister an absent or failed
edge; retain one removal per successfully registered transport.

Uke OEM 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd and OnePlus
fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba already guard the GLINK null edge.
Palawan 0d9f7fdf720ae9f4ecfbee4fadaf1e3b5c442e95, upstream
4056b3c9d3c92ea45955641dbafeb9b960e146ef and signed Linux 7.2.12 omit
that guard in the native callbacks. Retain native crash policy; do not copy
Android notifier/recovery behavior. This does not reorder DMA teardown or
claim complete remoteproc removal safety.

Signed-off-by: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
index aaac807..95be3ae 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
@@ -226,7 +226,8 @@ static void glink_subdev_stop(struct rproc_subdev *subdev, bool crashed)
 {
 	struct qcom_rproc_glink *glink = to_glink_subdev(subdev);
 
-	qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(glink->edge))
+		qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
 	glink->edge = NULL;
 }
 
@@ -339,7 +340,8 @@ static void smd_subdev_stop(struct rproc_subdev *subdev, bool crashed)
 {
 	struct qcom_rproc_subdev *smd = to_smd_subdev(subdev);
 
-	qcom_smd_unregister_edge(smd->edge);
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(smd->edge))
+		qcom_smd_unregister_edge(smd->edge);
 	smd->edge = NULL;
 }
 
